From 24cdf826839257518c740ac6979c7b7e7647c9f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:18:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] ARM: dts: am335x-bone: add the BeagleBone VVDN camera
 cape overlay

Add a device tree overlay for the BeagleBone 1.2MP camera cape (RadiumBoards
BB-BONE-CAM-VVDN): a QuickLogic CSSP camera interface on GPMC chip select 1
with an onsemi (Aptina) MT9M114 sensor on I2C2. The CSSP's DMA request
arrives through the EDMA event crossbar (input 30), so the overlay also
moves the EDMA memcpy channels away from channel 20.

The cape EEPROM reports part number BB-BONE-CAM-VVDN and version 00A0, and
U-Boot's cape scanner loads <part>-<version>.dtbo from the device tree
directory, so the overlay is named after those instead of after the usual
am335x-* scheme. A combined am335x-bone DTB is built as well so that the
overlay is applied to a base and gets validated.

The overlay disables the eMMC controller because the eMMC shares
gpmc_csn1 and gpmc_ad0..7 with the cape. Black and Green boards with the
cape fitted must boot from microSD; the eMMC is not held in reset and
possible contention with an idle eMMC on the shared lines is untested.
BeagleBone Green Wireless is not supported (its WiFi uses gpmc_ad10..15).

Tested on a BeagleBone White only.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [cape EEPROM file naming for U-Boot's cape scanner]
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
